>> servings: 4
>> source: https://www.nemlig.com/opskrifter/lune-fajitas-med-kylling-og-avocado-98002880
>> course: Dinner, Main
>> cuisine: Mexican
>> method: Oven

Heat the oven to 180 °C fan and line a #baking sheet{} with baking paper.

Peel the @red onions{2}. Dice a quarter of one onion finely and slice the rest into thin wedges. Keep the dice for the tomato salsa.

Rinse the @red bell peppers{2} and slice them into thin strips.

On a separate cutting board, slice the @chicken breast fillet{450%g} into strips.

Put the onion, bell pepper and chicken on the baking sheet. Add a good splash of @neutral oil{}, the @fajita seasoning{5%tsp}, @salt{} and @pepper{} and toss everything well.

Bake in the oven for about ~bake{15%minutes}, stirring a couple of times along the way.

Rinse the @lime{1} and grate the zest. Cut the lime into wedges.

Slice the @red cabbage{0.5} as finely as you can, preferably on a #mandoline{}, mind your fingers.

Put the red cabbage in a #bowl{} and toss it with half of the lime zest and juice, then sprinkle with a little salt. Massage the cabbage with your fingers until it softens and collapses.

Rinse and chop the @cherry tomatoes{200%g} and mix them with the finely diced red onion from earlier.

Add a little lime juice and season the salsa with salt, pepper and a pinch of @sugar{}.

Warm the @tortilla wraps{8} in the oven for about ~warm tortillas{2%minutes}, until they are warm and soft.

Serve the tortillas with the red cabbage slaw and the chicken fajita. Top with the fresh tomato salsa.
